-- Every police station in Georgia from OpenStreetMap (amenity=police, 2026-09-16),
-- as pins for the map's "Police" layer. Abkhazia and the Tskhinvali region are
-- excluded (point-in-polygon against their OSM boundaries) — a tourist cannot
-- get there and those posts cannot help them. Objects mapped twice within 60 m
-- (node + building outline) were merged, and points within 80 m of the three
-- hand-curated Tbilisi stations were skipped in their favour.
--
-- Names: OSM's English name when it has one, otherwise "Police station (town)".
-- The Georgian name, when OSM has it, is kept in front of the address so the
-- tourist can show it to a local or a taxi driver. Reverse-geocoded street and
-- settlement come from Nominatim. open_24h is true only where OSM says 24/7.
-- Idempotent: re-running refreshes the rows instead of failing on the key, and
-- ids carry the OSM id (n = node, w = way, r = relation) so a later re-import
-- updates the same rows.

on conflict (id) do update set name=excluded.name, type=excluded.type, address=excluded.address, lat=excluded.lat, lng=excluded.lng, open_24h=excluded.open_24h;
